Nick rejected a narrative opening in the LIMSOC incident categorisation pack ("Ask two experienced operators... That is not their fault.") as "too casual. I still want it to read like documentation / a proposal."

**Why:** These packs go to operations leadership, SME groups, and volunteer leadership for formal endorsement. Storytelling structure (problem stories, precedent, worked examples) is wanted, but the register must stay documentary.

**How to apply:** In LSV/SLSA/organisational proposal artefacts: no direct address ("ask two operators", "you will get"), no rhetorical question-and-answer constructions, no sentence fragments for punch ("Open wide, close narrow."), no colour details ("at 2am"), no colloquial idiom ("makes the right way the easy way", "speaking the same language"). Keep the stories and reasons-why, phrased as formal statements. Related: [[feedback-cover-letter-craft]] (different register: cover letters stay warm/narrative).
